    <title>Scotland: With J, M, A and H</title>
    <published>2026-03-17T00:00:00+00:00</published>
    <updated>2026-03-17T00:00:00+00:00</updated>
    <author>
      <name></name>
    </author>
    <link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="/travel/scotland/"/>
    <id>/travel/scotland/</id>
    
    <content type="html" xml:base="/travel/scotland/">&lt;p&gt;A plan made by the people, for the people with help from the people.
Image by &lt;a rel=&quot;external&quot; href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;unsplash.com&#x2F;photos&#x2F;train-on-bridge-surrounded-with-trees-at-daytime-XVoyX7l9ocY&quot;&gt;Jack Anstey&lt;&#x2F;a&gt; from Unsplashed.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;rough-plan&quot;&gt;Rough Plan&lt;&#x2F;h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Total trip time 10-14 days.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;4-5 days in Edinburgh.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remaining time trekking and exploring nature.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferably no car needed, as there&#x27;s car set malarkey.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;general-useful-info&quot;&gt;General Useful Info&lt;&#x2F;h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;callout callout-quote&quot;&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;For day trips I think Glasgow is the better option. Lots of public transport connections into Loch Lomond &amp;amp; The Trossachs National Park. You can also head over to Ayr and Dunoon easily by train then ferry and lots of nice hikes at both.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;

  &lt;cite&gt;— skifans from Reddit&lt;&#x2F;cite&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;People at &lt;a rel=&quot;external&quot; href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.haggisadventures.com&#x2F;blog&#x2F;how-to-5-days-in-scotland-without-a-car&quot;&gt;Off Kilter&lt;&#x2F;a&gt; have pretty much designed a trip for us.&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;days-1-4&quot;&gt;Days 1-4&lt;&#x2F;h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flying from MN into Edinburgh (sometime mid july).&lt;&#x2F;p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;days-5-10&quot;&gt;Days 5-10&lt;&#x2F;h2&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;references&quot;&gt;References&lt;&#x2F;h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a rel=&quot;external&quot; href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.reddit.com&#x2F;r&#x2F;hiking&#x2F;comments&#x2F;1kmdwmb&#x2F;hiking_spots_in_scotland_without_a_car&#x2F;&quot;&gt;Good Reddit Thread&lt;&#x2F;a&gt;&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a rel=&quot;external&quot; href=&quot;https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.haggisadventures.com&#x2F;blog&#x2F;how-to-5-days-in-scotland-without-a-car&quot;&gt;Off Kilter&lt;&#x2F;a&gt;&lt;&#x2F;li&gt;
&lt;&#x2F;ol&gt;
